{
 "comment": "Boss roster in progression order. Every 5th round spawns the next boss; after the last, the list loops with the loopMultiplier applied to hp/damage. Patterns: kingslime, charger, worm, shooter, stomper, wall. Each boss names the biomes it is fought in; the arena moves to one of them when it appears. Each boss also names the arena it is fought in, chosen for how it moves rather than its theme: worms and the wall get a bare corridor because terrain only traps you, chargers get open sky, and the stomper gets a low roof. Each boss also carries 'phases': thresholds where it changes how it fights, the way Terraria's bosses all do. A phase merges its 'config' over the pattern config, may replace 'shoot' outright, and may switch 'pattern' entirely (Plantera stops hovering and gives chase). Thresholds are fractions of maximum health, listed high to low, and a fight never goes back up a phase. Each boss also carries 'drops': the pool its treasure bag offers. A kill drops a bag, and walking over it deals three of these face up to choose from -- one free, and the other two lost. Pools are real Terraria drops wherever the item exists here, tier matched to the round the boss is actually beaten on.",
 "loopMultiplier": {
  "hp": 1.6,
  "damage": 1.35
